<title>TUNISIA: Tunisia to issue hydrocarbons code next year.</title>
<headline>Tunisia to issue hydrocarbons code next year.</headline>
<dateline>TUNIS 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>A new hydrocarbons code aimed at giving more incentives for oil firms to invest in the Tunisian energy sector would be issued next year, Industry Minister Slaheddine Bouguerra said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The new hydrocarbons code should be adopted in 1997,&quot; Bouguerra told the Fifth Tunisian Petroleum Exploration Conference.</p>
<p>Fourty two oil firms are currently operating in Tunisia in 40 permits. Tunisia this year granted international oil firms six new permits for exploration.</p>
<p>The North African country produced 4.3 milion tonnes of crude in 1995.</p>
<p>--Tunis newsroom, 2161-787538</p>
</text>
